# cuts/v1.0.55/cut.env -- the pins this cut is made from.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY v1.0.55, AND WHY IT IS NOT A RE-RUN OF v1.0.54
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.54 was tagged at 42464845 on 2026-09-01T17:46:14Z. Its PREFLIGHT PASSED
# -- the same gate that refused v1.0.53 four times -- and the cut job then
# failed at 17:48:16Z inside the build, at `make check-orphans`:
#
#     [RED]  CM051:#1305   OPEN PR 'the SHIPPING ostler_fda has never written
#                          a record' is NOT in origin/main
#     [RED]  CM051:#1300   OPEN PR 'bind WHAT DID THE WALKING (harness_commit)'
#                          is NOT in origin/main
#     make: *** [check-orphans] Error 1
#
# 🔴 THAT IS A DIFFERENT DEATH FROM v1.0.53 AND THE DISTINCTION DECIDES THE FIX.
# v1.0.53 failed on four conditions of the tree at its own commit, so it was
# born dead: no re-run could ever pass. v1.0.54 died on a gate that is NOT part
# of preflight and that reads state OUTSIDE the tree. So the honest question is
# not "was the tag stale" but "can this gate be satisfied without moving the
# tag", and the answer is no -- for a reason worth writing down.
#
# THE GATE OFFERS TWO REMEDIES AND THEY ARE NOT SYMMETRIC:
#
#   MERGE the PRs      check-orphans resolves its ship ref as `origin/main`
#                      (scripts/verify_no_orphaned_fixes.sh:1009) and reads
#                      live PR state at BUILD time. Merging to main WOULD have
#                      turned it green on a re-run of the v1.0.54 tag -- while
#                      the DMG, built from that tag, still did not contain the
#                      merged work. 🔴 THAT GREEN WAS AVAILABLE AND WAS REFUSED.
#                      It is the gate passing on the premise "origin/main is
#                      what we ship", which is false for any tag that is not
#                      main's head, and it would have produced an artefact the
#                      gate believed complete and which was not.
#
#   DEFER the PRs      cut-deferrals.yaml is read from ${REPO_ROOT} -- the TREE
#                      (same script, line 63). A deferral row is therefore a
#                      commit, and a commit cannot precede the tag that would
#                      have to contain it. Unreachable for v1.0.54 for exactly
#                      the v1.0.53 reason.
#
# Both honest routes need a commit the v1.0.54 tag cannot hold, so the version
# moves. Deferral was chosen: neither PR is ready, MEASURED on a latest-check-
# run-per-name histogram -- #1305 is 2 failing of 66, #1300 is 4 failing of 36.
# Merging a red PR to clear a ship gate is the move cut-deferrals.yaml exists
# to prevent.
#
# ⚠️ NOTE FOR THE NEXT CUT: check-orphans is NOT a preflight gate. It runs
# inside the build, after signing begins, and it reads LIVE GitHub state. Any
# PR opened in CM051 or the daemon repo between tag and build can kill a cut
# that preflight has already cleared. Sweep open PRs immediately before tagging.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.54 IS NOT DELETED, FOR THE SAME REASON v1.0.53 IS NOT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# It published nothing -- no release object, no bytes, no DMG, and nobody
# installed it. But the ref truthfully records a tree that was tagged and
# refused, and force-repointing it would make ONE VERSION NAME TWO TREES, which
# is the class this project filed against itself. Versions are cheap. Recorded
# not_walked in cuts/DEFECTS_ROLLFORWARD.md, 0 findings.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PINS ARE UNCHANGED FROM v1.0.54, DELIBERATELY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# main was still AT 42464845 when the cut died, so nothing shipping moved
# between the two versions. DAEMON_COMMIT and CM051 below are the same values
# v1.0.54 carried, and the four BOM rows sit at the same four refs.
#
# DAEMON_COMMIT c6fc48c0 -> hub-v0.4.69, published to BOTH halves:
#   ostler-ai/ostler-releases    ostler-assistant-...-v0.4.69.tar.gz
#                                sha256 e680396893fadd78...fc92a84f
#                                Developer-ID signed, notarised, stapled
#   ostler-ai/ostler-assistant   ostler-hub-app-...-v0.4.69.tar.gz
#                                sha256 3e030adb594c5f73...2ab2a8b8
#                                ADHOC BY DESIGN -- the cut re-signs it
#
# 🔴 TWO REPOS, ONE TAG. Both are fetched at $(DAEMON_RELEASE_TAG); publishing
# one half leaves the cut 404ing on the other, and the hub-app fetch path is
# never taken on an operator's Mac, so a missing half is invisible locally and
# fails in a clean room. Both halves were verified published with a 404 control
# on each repository before v1.0.54 was tagged; that evidence stands unchanged
# because neither the tag nor the digests have moved.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT THIS CUT CARRIES -- ONE customer-visible fix, and saying so matters
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# oa #369 = Andy's #454 from the v1.0.52 hand walk: "we agreed that there
# wouldn't be this 'Advanced' section". The Advanced surface is gone from
# Settings and its two customer-facing controls -- the daily-brief schedule and
# the iMessage message prefix -- are mounted on Preferences, so nothing is lost.
# Deleting the link alone would have re-created #877, where those controls were
# orphaned with no route to them.
#
# DOES NOT CARRY -- five of Andy's six v1.0.52 findings (rollforward rows
# v1052-D001..D006), and now also CM051 #1305, the producer that would make the
# SHIPPING ostler_fda write a usage record at all. The Bursar roster is
# therefore still short: three of five required producers write nothing on any
# install. A4 is Andy's scope call and is not being coded around.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NO WALK RECORD AT THE MOMENT THIS IS MADE, AND THAT IS CORRECT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# walks/v1.0.55.tsv does not exist, so verify_walk_record.sh returns rc=2 --
# absence, correctly not conflated with badness -- PROMOTE=0, the release is a
# prerelease, and ostler.ai/install.dmg keeps resolving to its current target.
# The sequence is cut -> walk -> record -> only then promote.
#
# ⚠️ PUT THE DMG IN THE WALKED ACCOUNT'S ~/Downloads. post_walk_qa.sh looks in
# only $HOME/Downloads, $HOME/Desktop and $HOME of the ssh user it walks as, and
# on a CLEAN record the gate then REQUIRES artefact_sha256_source to read
# measured(...). A clean walk whose DMG sits elsewhere produces PROMOTE=0 for a
# reason that reads as "no walk evidence" rather than "wrong folder".

CUT_VERSION=1.0.55
DAEMON_COMMIT=c6fc48c0
CM051=8f66b632c2b8ecba74eb4147b9bd05edebae5d59
